WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:08.139
This is the Mann family from Cornwall - and
these are their provisions.

00:00:08.139 --> 00:00:14.059
Food and drink for several months for five
people plus their cat and dog - just in case:

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:20.140
there's the worst case.We're not stocking
up for war, but for Brexit.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.180
The Manns have always been against Britain
leaving the EU.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.140
And everything they've heard from London in
the last two years makes them think Brexit

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.980
is going to be a chaotic process.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.310
They've bought a water tank with filter and
because the UK gets some of its electricity

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:48.679
from Europe, they're getting ready

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:52.999
for power cuts.

00:00:52.999 --> 00:00:55.999
The whole family helps out with the weeding.

00:00:55.999 --> 00:00:59.460
They hope that their home-grown greens will
soon be ready to eat.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.449
Is all this a bit too much?

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:03.809
Maybe.

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:08.000
But midwife Nevine says they are simply going
on what they've heard from their government.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:17.110
Die Regierung hat jetzt gesagt, es könnten
sechs Monate werden in denen nur 15 - 20 % der

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.770
Importe ins Land kommen.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:23.740
Bislang haben wir gedacht, dass wir Lebensmittel
für drei Monate brauchen werden.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.640
Deshalb kaufen wir jetzt noch mehr ein.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.719
Wir hatten das Problem unterschätzt.

00:01:28.719 --> 00:01:32.920
The Mann family say they only rely on themselves.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.740
Others haven't yet given up the fight yet.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.759
It's early morning in London and a group of
young people are about to get on a campaign

00:01:39.759 --> 00:01:41.079
bus.

00:01:41.079 --> 00:01:44.659
Their organisation is called 'Our future,
our choice'.

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:48.149
Just like 59 percent of the British population,
they want a second referendum.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:50.469
Es gibt so viel zu tun.

00:01:50.469 --> 00:01:56.250
In ein paar Jahren werden wir zurückblicken
und uns fragen, ob wir damals genug getan

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.250
haben.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.570
Der Wind hat sich gedreht.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.890
Jetzt haben wir wirklich eine Chance.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:06.749
According to polls, some 77 percent of Britons
under the age of 24 would vote against leaving

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:08.509
the EU.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:12.240
And every day, more young people are becoming
old enough to vote.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:20.019
The message that these ativists are promoting
- 'Please Stand Up for Our Future.

00:02:20.019 --> 00:02:22.459
'
The Mann family in Cornwall have long since

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:25.900
given up hoping Britain will remain in the
EU.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.849
They don't think it going to end well either
- so they're heading back to the shops to

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.549
stock up on more food.

